          "bbox": [
            0.238,
            0.065,
            0.883,
            0.123
          ],
          "content": "Broad straps reduce the pressure exerted by the bag onNarrow our shoulders as compared to narrow straps. Therefore, we feel more comfortable carrying a bag with broad straps."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.05,
            0.193,
            0.274,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.043,
                0.143,
                0.268,
                0.175
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 6.2: Buckets with broad and narrow handles"
            },
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.096,
                0.38,
                0.23,
                0.413
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 6.3: Persons carrying loads"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.283,
            0.123,
            0.884,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": "Can you now understand why it feels easier to lift a water-filled bucket with a broad handle than with a narrow handle (Fig. 6.2)? Similarly, we have seen that when people carry loads like pots or vegetable baskets on their heads, they often place a round piece of cloth under the loads (Fig. 6.3). In both cases, the objective is to reduce pressure by increasing the area over which the weight acts."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.254,
            0.883,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": "Pressure is defined as the force per unit area. The **SI unit** of **force** is **newton** and that of **area** is **metre**<strong><sup>2</sup></strong>. Therefore, the **SI unit** of **pressure** is **newton/metre2 (N/m2**). This unit is also called a **pascal**, denoted by **Pa**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.283,
            0.329,
            0.882,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "If a force of 100 N is applied on a cardboard of area 2 m<sup>2</sup>, then the pressure applied on the cardboard will be:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.421,
            0.376,
            0.744,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{pressure} = \\frac{\\mathrm{Fore}}{\\mathrm{Area}} = \\frac{100\\mathrm{~N}}{2\\mathrm{~m}^2} = 50\\mathrm{~N/m}^2",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.416,
            0.885,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": "There are many situations in daily life where pressure plays a role. **Conduct** the activities given in Table 6.1 and **record** your observations. **Explain** how pressure influences the mode of action undertaken for each activity."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.495,
            0.279,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
